an white  irregular shaped  firm mass  which is present underneath the skin ellipse and comes to 0 1cm from the closest posterior resection margin  Also identified 0 6cm medial to the mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan white  firm  irregular shaped nodule  which comes to 0 5cm from the closest posterior inferior margin  A 0 3cm additional tan white nodule is present adjacent to the second irregular nodule and comes to 0 5cm from the anterior inferior margin  The breast parenchyma away from the nodules is tan white  rubbery  without additional lesions  Section Code  B  The mass with the posterior resection margin  C   D  Additional sections of the mass  E  The second nodule with the posterior inferior resection margin  F  The second nodule with the anterior resection margin  G  The third nodule with the anterior resection margin  H  The breast parenchyma  away from the nodules  In the axillary tail  measuring 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  four nodules  measuring 0 5cm in diameter to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm in diameter  are present  The two smallest nodules are entirely submitted in cassette I  The largest two nodules are bivalved and entirely submitted in cassette J  Labeled   additional superficial tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0 7cm fibrofatty tissue  which is sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes K and L  Labeled   additional axillary tissue   is a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan white node with attached adipose tissue  The specimen is bivalved and entirely submitted in cassette M  Resident  Mari Mino  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL   EXCISION  FOCAL HISTIOCYTOSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  SARAH ROLLINS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL  HOT   BLUE  PA