ns  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistently shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 91 at 17 34     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  51 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  107 fm mg cytosolic protein Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received on ice  labeled  Left breast mass   is a 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1cm  gritty  ill defined nodule approaching to within 0 3cm of the nearest margin  A representative section is frozen as Frozen Section  1 and saved frozen  Tissue is submitted for Estrogen receptors and BRDU studies  The remainder of the tissue is submitted in A through K  Resident  Robert F  Cheek  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Elizabeth Bailey  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Steven Ralph Levisohn  M D  David William Rattner  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS BIOPSY , No.
