Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Resident  Alton Brad Farris III  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Right nipple duct excision  Rule out papilloma  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT NIPPLE DUCT   EXCISION  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 1 TO FOCAL 2  WITH FOCUS HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR EARLY INVASION  SEE NOTE  2  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   NOTE  One slightly irregular focus of carcinoma almost completely lacks a myoepithelial cell layer  as seen on p63  smooth muscle myosin  and calponin immunostains  A cytokeratin stain highlights the irregularities in contour  This area spans about 0 1cm and is favored to represent early blunt invasion arising out of ductal carcinoma in situ  Other nests of carcinoma also demonstrate large gaps in the myoepithelial cell layer  perhaps representing an earlier stage of the same phenomenon  The ductal carcinoma in situ involves 8 of 12 blocks and is focally positive at the inked margin  as well as being  0 1cm from the inked margin along a broad front  Calcifications are present in the ductal carcinoma in situ and in vessels  Multiple levels examined  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right nipple duct rule out papilloma   is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm excisional breast biopsy specimen consisting of tan yellow  lobulated fatty tissue with focal hemorrhage externally  The specimen is not oriented  The external surface is inked black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal somewhat firm  ill defined tissue in the central portion of the specimen distinct from the surrounding yellow  lobulated fatty  soft tissue  The ill defined region is somewhat firm and tan white  The ill defined region focally abuts the margin  One potential duct is identified 0 2cm in diameter  and multiple potential small ducts are identified which measures 0 1cm in diameter  The largest potential duct contains mucoid material  The specimen is entirely submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Ends of specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Firm tissue from central portion of specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue containing ducts from central portion of specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of specimen  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  No definitive invasive tumor cells are seen in the tissue sections for receptor stains   See note   Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show 