la at the opposite end of the skin ellipse  In the center of the areola with a 1 0cm in diameter unremarkable nipple 0 5cm inferior to the nipple is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm apparent acrochordon on the areola  1 7cm from the areolar margin  Also received in the same container is a separate 15 x 4 5cm skin ellipse  with 2cm of underlying adipose tissue  Both the skin and the adipose tissue are unremarkable  The mastectomy specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm area of fibrous tissue beneath the scar  The fibrous tissue beneath the scar extends to 3 5cm from the deep resection margin and 3 0cm from the closest lateral resection margin  Within the remainder of the breast parenchyma are focal areas of rubbery tan breast parechyma  No firm  stellate  or gritty area are identified  SECTION CODE  A  skin with scar B  nipple C  acrochordon on areola D G  sections of biopsy site with inked margins H M  additional sections of breast parenchyma distant from biopsy site N U  lymph nodes from axillary tale V  representative section of separate skin ellipse  Resident  Jeoffry Brennick  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  David Bent Smith  M D  James M Fitzgerald  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST AND AXILLA   report_end  , Yes.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  04 AUG 98 at 13 19 CLINICAL DATA  Previous history right breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor is focally less than 0 1cm from an inked margin  Vascular or lymphatic invasion are not seen  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  06 AUG 98 at 19 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 98 at 13 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue which is unoriented  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal an ill defined  firm white  focally cystic area which is entirely submitted in cassette A  The remainder of the specimen is grossly unremarkable and is entirely submitted in cassette B  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  SELIM NASSER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , No.
