Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 04 CLINICAL DATA  Calcification on x ray                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  80    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION AS MEASURED ON A GLASS SLIDE  PRESENT AT INKED LATERAL RESECTION MARGIN  WITH MULTIPLE FOCI OF LYMPHATIC INVASION  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  20    SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES WITH HIGH GRADE NUCLEI AND NECROSIS  WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATION  PRESENT ADJACENT TO INVASIVE CARCINOMA  PRESENT AT INKED RESECTION MARGIN IN SEVERAL AREAS  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 59                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of breast tissue  Inked black  A long stitch designates the lateral surface  inked yellow over black  A short stitch designates the superior surface inked green over black  Sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm white firm nodular area within 0 3cm of the closest resection margin  radiating in multiple series of white bands reaching the excised surface in multiple points  Representative sections submitted in cassettes A through J  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Yes.
