ent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm breast tissue with a suture designating the deep margin  The deep resection margin is inked black  and the superficial resection margin is inked blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 2 5cm in maximal diameter pink gray  firm nodule that abuts the superficial resection margin and is deeply covered only by a thin rim of fibrous tissue  A second separate nodule  0 4cm in maximal diameter is also identified  A representative section of the large nodule in relation to both the superficial and deep resection margin is frozen as FX 1  now in cassette A  A representative section of the small nodule is frozen as FX 2  now in cassette G  Section code  A  large nodule  previously frozen as FX 1 B F large nodule  additional sections G  small nodule  previously frozen as FX 2 H  small nodule  entirely submitted I  grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST LARGE NODULE   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2   LEFT BREAST  SMALL NODULE   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , No.
