 reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 9cm area of fibrosis underlying the skin scar  extending to within 0 4cm of the posterior margin  At the superior and medial edge of the scar is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan white firm  round  poorly defined mass which is 0 9cm from the posterior margin  A metal surgical clip is identified within this scar  The remainder of the specimen is composed of yellow tan lobulated adipose tissue with unremarkable tan pink fibrous tissue  No axillary tail is present  and no lymph nodes are identified in the upper outer quadrant  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Entire mass at edge of scar  with relation to posterior margin  C  Scar with closest posterior margin  D  Scar and posterior margin  E  Fibrous area adjacent to scar  F  Unremarkable breast from lower inner quadrant  G H  Additional firm nodule  I L  Possible lymph nodes from upper outer quadrant  Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm portion of yellow tan adipose tissue  Serial sectioning reveals no abnormalities  No sections are submitted  Resident  PAUL N  STAATS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Jonathan Michael Winograd  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 41 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast lesion                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  60   AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  40    FOCALLY COMEDO TYPE  MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  WITH FOCAL MICROSCOPIC EXTENSION TO AN INKED MARGIN  2  MICROCALCIFICATION  3  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  NOTE  The invasive carcinoma measures about 1cm in greatest diameter on the microscopic slide  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 53                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  Right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibrous  fatty tissue with an accompanying x ray showing calcifications in the right breast  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing a slightly gritty  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  ill defined  tan mass with focal grumous  yellow material  This lesion is present at the ink  Another nodule  0 4cm in greatest dimension  is present distally  3mm from the ink  The larger nodule is submitted in A and B  the smaller nodule in C  the remainder in D and E  No frozen section was performed  Resident  Jo Ann E  Haney  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS GROSS  RIGHT BREAST LESION   SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA   TOO SMALL FOR FROZEN SECTION  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Elizabeth Bailey  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST LESION   report_end  , No.
