TE x 2 5cm containing an unremarkable nipple measuring 1 4cm in greatest diameter  The specimen has been oriented by the surgeon with a short stitch designating the superior aspect and a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  The anterior aspect is inked blue  the posterior is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a hemorrhagic excisional cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The cavity is located 0 2cm from the anterior aspect and 1 0cm from the posterior margin of resection  The remainder of the specimen is notable only for blue injection dye  The remainder of the specimen consists of yellow adipose tissue with white fibrous parenchyma  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial aspect of biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Full thickness cross section of biopsy cavity including to anterior and posterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Full thickness cross section of excisional cavity including anterior and posterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Further sections of excisional cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lobulated breast parenchyma  upper outer   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lobular breast parenchyma  inferior to biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lobulated breast parenchyma  inferior to biopsy cavity  Received fresh  labeled  additional margin  right   are multiple fragments of yellow fibroadipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The specimen is received unoriented  the external surface is inked black  and the specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  additional margin  left   are multiple fragments of yellow tan adipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The specimen is received unoriented  the external surface is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received are 2 additional containers which are  labeled REMOVE_