Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 55 CLINICAL DATA  None provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION     INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  WITH NEUROENDOCRINE DIFFERENTIATION  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN     DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH NEUROENDOCRINE DIFFERENTIATION  NOTE  The tumor measures 0 9cm in greatest diameter  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  PAS and Grimelius stains show intracytoplasmic granules confirming the neuroendocrine nature of the tumor  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 07                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm fragment of breast tissue  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a hard  stellate  centrally hemorrhagic  white tan lesion  0 9cm in greatest dimension  and 0 1cm from inked margin  No frozen is done  and the specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through H with  the lesion in cassettes C through E  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST MASS   SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edward M Barksdale  M D  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , No.
