Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 09 39 CLINICAL DATA  History of infiltrating ductal carcinoma of right breast in  REMOVED_CASE_ID                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  75    REMOVED_DATE CM  MULTIFOCAL  PRESENT ON 5 OF 6 SLIDES  EXTENDING TO ANTERIOR AND SUPERIOR MARGINS ALONG BROAD FRONTS  NEGATIVE FOR LYMPHOVASCULAR INVASION  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  25    PRESENT ON 3 OF 6 SLIDES  EXTENDING TO A SUPERIOR MARGIN  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 06                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained w